00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.570
- [Instructor] In this
video, we're going to see

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:06.570
if we can compute what three
divided by 0.75 is equal to,

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.850
and I'll give you a little bit of a hint

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.830
before I tell you to pause the video.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:19.420
So let's imagine three
wholes right over here,

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.430
and what if we were to
think of these three wholes,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.560
these three ones, and what if we were to

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.990
think about them in terms of hundredths?

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.000
Well then we could, once we
express these as hundredths,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.590
we could say, well how many
groups of 75 hundredths

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.990
can we divide this into?

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.570
How many equal groups of 75 hundredths?

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.020
To help you think about that,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.580
here's a little bit of a visualization

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:48.580
where three is divided into
equal groups of 75 hundredths.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.960
So pause this video and use what I have,

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.760
this little visual here, as a big hint

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.253
to figure out what three
divided by 75/100 is.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.660
All right, now let's do it together.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.830
So as I said, we started with three ones,

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.170
or three wholes, however
you want to think about it,

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.290
and you could divide division by 75/100

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:15.530
as saying, well how many
equal groups of 75 hundredths

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.760
can you divide these three wholes into?

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.930
And so we thought about these three wholes

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.490
in terms of hundredths, and
the way it's been color coded,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.550
it actually has already been divided

00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:30.420
into four equal groups of 75 hundredths.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.830
You can count these, so this is

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:35.500
10, 20, 30, 40,

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.710
50, 60, 70,

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.900
and then five hundredths.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.900
So this right over here, this
is one group of 75 hundredths.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.360
Then in green you have another
group of 75 hundredths.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.050
So you have 10, 20, 30,

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.137
40, 50, 60, 70,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.710
and then 75, so that right over,

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.380
let me use a color I can see.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.560
This right over here is our second group.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.620
This is our first group right over there.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.610
Then that's our third group,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.490
these are all equal
groups of 75 hundredths,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.690
and that's our fourth equal group

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.570
of 75 hundredths in the green again.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.170
So how many equal groups of 75 hundredths

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.970
can you divide three wholes into?

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:30.633
Well, clearly it is equal to four.

